spec: S02-01, S02-02, S02-03, S02-06, S02-10, S02-12, S02-13, S02-17, S17-03, S17-08

Seeds the Documents the read-only `40-docs` cases look at: `ro-plan` (v1 → v2 via `--doc`
by Name → v3 = v1's content again, pushed from the stale v1 Sidecar: refused with the missing
change shown (ticket 17), then pushed over it with `--discard-head-changes`), two Documents named
`dup-plan`, a deleted `ro-del`, and `lst-a/b/c` for list order.
Merged stdout+stderr; ids are random.

```console
$ annotary -p rowan push ro-plan.md -m "first draft"
ro-plan	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push ro-plan-v2/ro-plan.md --doc ro-plan -m "add risks"
ro-plan	[..]	v2

$ annotary -p rowan push ro-plan.md -m "back to v1"
? 5
error: v2 by @rowan changed ro-plan.md since your v1 — those changes are not in your file — put them into ro-plan.md and push again
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
 # Plan
 
 We ship the CLI before the web UI.
+
+## Risks
+
+None yet.

$ annotary -p rowan push ro-plan.md -m "back to v1" --discard-head-changes
warning: discarding v2 by @rowan since your v1
ro-plan	[..]	v3 (same content as v1)

$ annotary -p rowan push a/dup-plan.md
dup-plan	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p agent push b/dup-plan.md
dup-plan	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push ro-del.md
ro-del	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan delete ro-del
ro-del	[..]	deleted

$ annotary -p rowan push lst-b.md
lst-b	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push lst-c.md
lst-c	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push lst-a.md
lst-a	[..]	v1

```
